From: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
Subject: [PATCH] tools: mtk_image: honour SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH

mtk_image_set_mt7621_header() reads the wall clock and writes it to the
timestamp of the legacy image header. The MT7621 boot loader image
therefore differs on every build.

Use imagetool_get_source_date(), which the other image tools already use,
and keep the wall clock as the fallback.

Signed-off-by: John Crispin <john@phrozen.org>
---
 tools/mtk_image.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/tools/mtk_image.c
+++ b/tools/mtk_image.c
@@ -706,7 +706,7 @@ static void mtk_image_set_mt7621_header(
 	shdr->stage_size = cpu_to_be32(datasize);

 	image_set_magic(hdr, IH_MAGIC);
-	image_set_time(hdr, time(NULL));
+	image_set_time(hdr, imagetool_get_source_date("mtk_image", time(NULL)));
 	image_set_size(hdr, datasize);
 	image_set_load(hdr, loadaddr);
 	image_set_ep(hdr, loadaddr);
